    .wk-step-in { --wk-shift: 16px; }
  }

  /* ── HIDING, LAST AND SPELLED OUT ─────────────────────────────────────────
     This rule was higher up once and two layers ignored it completely: the
     model pair and the panels, which set `display: grid` and `display: flex`
     through `.wk-layer.is-pair` and `.wk-layer.is-panel`. Both are class +
     class, which after Astro appends its scope attribute weighs exactly the
     same as class + attribute — a tie, broken by source order, and they came
     later. The stage drew three layers on top of each other at every step.

     So the rule sits at the very end and names every selector it has to beat,
     rather than reaching for !important. Anything added later that sets
     `display` on a layer has to be added here too, which is the point: it is a
     list you cannot forget quietly. */
